= Appendix J — The Trap File

Each contrast is a reminder to read what the question actually asks. A familiar word can be correct in one setting and wrong in another.

#table(columns: (1fr, 1fr, 2.2fr), inset: 5pt, stroke: 0.5pt + jamb-border,
  table.header([*Do not confuse*], [*With*], [*The distinction*]),
  [Data], [information], [Data are raw facts; information is data interpreted in a useful context.],
  [Difference Engine], [Analytical Engine], [One was intended for tables; the other was a more general programmable design.],
  [Analog], [digital], [Analog represents continuously varying quantities; digital uses discrete values.],
  [General-purpose], [digital], [Purpose and form of data are different classifications.],
  [CPU], [system unit], [The CPU is a processor; the system unit contains several components.],
  [Input], [output], [Input supplies data; output presents results. A touchscreen can do both.],
  [OCR], [OMR], [OCR recognises characters; OMR detects marks in specified positions.],
  [OMR], [MICR], [OMR detects marks; MICR reads special magnetic-ink characters.],
  [RAM], [SSD], [RAM is ordinarily volatile working memory; an SSD provides non-volatile storage.],
  [Cache], [backup], [Cache supports faster access; a backup is a separate recoverable copy.],
  [Bit], [byte], [A byte contains eight bits.],
  [kB], [KiB], [The decimal kB is 1,000 bytes; a KiB is 1,024 bytes. Follow the question's convention.],
  [Binary 10], [decimal 10], [Binary 10 represents decimal two.],
  [Hexadecimal 10], [decimal 10], [Hexadecimal 10 represents decimal sixteen.],
  [System software], [application software], [The OS manages resources; applications carry out user tasks.],
  [Freeware], [open source], [Zero price does not itself grant source-code modification or redistribution rights.],
  [Copy], [move], [Copy creates another item; move changes the item's location.],
  [Save], [backup], [Saving changes is not necessarily creating a separate recoverable copy.],
  [UPS], [surge protector], [A UPS can provide temporary power; a surge protector limits surges within its rating.],
  [Preventive], [corrective maintenance], [Preventive action precedes a fault; corrective action addresses one.],
  [LAN], [WAN], [A LAN covers a limited area; a WAN connects over a wider area.],
  [Internet], [web], [The web is a system of linked resources using the internet.],
  [Browser], [search engine], [A browser accesses web resources; a search engine helps locate indexed information.],
  [HTTPS], [site trustworthiness], [HTTPS protects the connection; it does not guarantee the operator is honest.],
